   "text": "ONE INTENT, END TO END \u2014 everything below step 0 runs on that room's single virtual thread",
   "fontSize": 19,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "ONE INTENT, END TO END \u2014 everything below step 0 runs on that room's single virtual thread",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "t95",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 95,
   "y": 1833,
   "width": 1118,
   "height": 260,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#334155",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 666,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1236,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1770000000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "0  gateway.onMessage(socket, json)          PlayerId actor = cookie.verify(socket);      // identity without an account\n     if (!registry.find(code).offer(new Submit(actor, payload, msgId))) socket.close(OVERLOADED);   // bounded queue IS the backpressure\n        |\n        v   RoomActor.run() -> handle(Submit)\n1     I intent = def.parseIntent(raw);                              // only the definition can turn JSON into an I\n      if (def.validate(state, intent, actor) instanceof Reject r) { broadcaster.toPlayer(actor, rejected(msgId, r)); return; }\n2     List<E> events = def.reduce(state, intent, ctx);              // pure; time and randomness arrive through ctx\n3     S next = events.stream().reduce(state, def::apply);           // FOLD FIRST \u2014 a throw here must not leave a log the state lacks\n      long at = ctx.now();  for (E e : events) seq = log.append(e, at, def.version());  this.state = next;   // swap only on success\n4     broadcaster.toRoom(code, viewsFor(next));                     // tell them it is their turn BEFORE the clock starts\n5     def.turn(next).ifPresentOrElse(t -> turnClock.arm(code, t, seq), () -> turnClock.cancel(code));   // seq = fencing token\n6     if (def.isHandComplete(next)) reveal(hand.serverSeed());\n\nRECONNECT  Command.Reconnect -> session.snapshotFor(viewer) -> send sync{seq, view}.  Snapshot only: no event tail, nothing to double-apply.\nVERIFY     re-derive the deal from the revealed seed and match it against what was broadcast. Folding the server's own log proves only\n           that apply() is deterministic \u2014 a rigged shuffle replays perfectly.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "0  gateway.onMessage(socket, json)          PlayerId actor = cookie.verify(socket);      // identity without an account\n     if (!registry.find(code).offer(new Submit(actor, payload, msgId))) socket.close(OVERLOADED);   // bounded queue IS the backpressure\n        |\n        v   RoomActor.run() -> handle(Submit)\n1     I intent = def.parseIntent(raw);                              // only the definition can turn JSON into an I\n      if (def.validate(state, intent, actor) instanceof Reject r) { broadcaster.toPlayer(actor, rejected(msgId, r)); return; }\n2     List<E> events = def.reduce(state, intent, ctx);              // pure; time and randomness arrive through ctx\n3     S next = events.stream().reduce(state, def::apply);           // FOLD FIRST \u2014 a throw here must not leave a log the state lacks\n      long at = ctx.now();  for (E e : events) seq = log.append(e, at, def.version());  this.state = next;   // swap only on success\n4     broadcaster.toRoom(code, viewsFor(next));                     // tell them it is their turn BEFORE the clock starts\n5     def.turn(next).ifPresentOrElse(t -> turnClock.arm(code, t, seq), () -> turnClock.cancel(code));   // seq = fencing token\n6     if (def.isHandComplete(next)) reveal(hand.serverSeed());\n\nRECONNECT  Command.Reconnect -> session.snapshotFor(viewer) -> send sync{seq, view}.  Snapshot only: no event tail, nothing to double-apply.\nVERIFY     re-derive the deal from the revealed seed and match it against what was broadcast. Folding the server's own log proves only\n           that apply() is deterministic \u2014 a rigged shuffle replays perfectly.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
