  {
   "id": "t98",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 95,
   "y": 2223,
   "width": 1062,
   "height": 146,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#78350f",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 687,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1275,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1770000000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1  oneWriterPerRoom()            Game state is mutated by exactly one thread and no lock protects it. Not \"no locks exist\" \u2014\n                                 ConcurrentHashMap and ArrayBlockingQueue hold plenty internally.\n2  stateIsSafelyPublished()      state is volatile and every S is DEEPLY immutable \u2014 a record holding an ArrayList is not.\n3  gameDefinitionIsStateless()   A definition is a ServiceLoader singleton shared by every room; one mutable field corrupts them all.\n4  sameSeedSameEvents()          Same seed + same intent sequence => byte-identical event sequence.\n5  illegalIntentIsTotalNoOp()    No event, no seq bump, no broadcast to anyone but the caller.\n6  projectionNeverLeaks()        No projected payload contains a card the viewer may not see. Property test over random states.\n   ArchUnit ban list for games:  currentTimeMillis \u00b7 nanoTime \u00b7 Instant.now \u00b7 LocalDate.now \u00b7 new Random() \u00b7 Math.random \u00b7\n                                 ThreadLocalRandom \u00b7 UUID.randomUUID()  <- the innocent one that silently destroys replay.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "1  oneWriterPerRoom()            Game state is mutated by exactly one thread and no lock protects it. Not \"no locks exist\" \u2014\n                                 ConcurrentHashMap and ArrayBlockingQueue hold plenty internally.\n2  stateIsSafelyPublished()      state is volatile and every S is DEEPLY immutable \u2014 a record holding an ArrayList is not.\n3  gameDefinitionIsStateless()   A definition is a ServiceLoader singleton shared by every room; one mutable field corrupts them all.\n4  sameSeedSameEvents()          Same seed + same intent sequence => byte-identical event sequence.\n5  illegalIntentIsTotalNoOp()    No event, no seq bump, no broadcast to anyone but the caller.\n6  projectionNeverLeaks()        No projected payload contains a card the viewer may not see. Property test over random states.\n   ArchUnit ban list for games:  currentTimeMillis \u00b7 nanoTime \u00b7 Instant.now \u00b7 LocalDate.now \u00b7 new Random() \u00b7 Math.random \u00b7\n                                 ThreadLocalRandom \u00b7 UUID.randomUUID()  <- the innocent one that silently destroys replay.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
 ],
